{"id":30364,"artist":"John Denver","title":"Take Me Home Country Roads","lyrics_plain":"Almost heaven, West Virginia\nBlue Ridge Mountains, Shanandoah River\nLife is old there, older than the trees\nYounger than the mountains, growing like a breeze\nCountry Roads, take me home\nTo the place, I belong\nWest Virginia, Mountain mama\nTake me home, Country Road\nAll my memories, gather 'round her\nMiner's lady, strangers to blue water\nDark and dusty, painted on the sky\nMisty taste of moonshine, tear drops in my eyes\nCountry Roads, take me home\nTo the place, I belong\nWest Virginia, Mountain mama\nTake me home, Country Road\nI hear her voice in the morning how she calls me,\nThe radio reminds me, of my home far away,\nAnd driving down the road, I get a feeling\nThat I should have been home, Yesterday, Yesterday.\nCountry Roads, take me home\nTo the place, I belong\nWest Virginia, Mountain mama\nTake me home Country Road\nCountry Roads, take me home\nTo the place, I belong\nWest Virginia, Mountain mama\nTake me home, Country Road\nTake me home, Country Road\nTake me home, Country Road.","lyrics_synced":"[00:38.62] Almost heaven, West Virginia\n[00:43.90] Blue Ridge Mountains, Shanandoah River\n[00:50.51] Life is old there, older than the trees\n[00:55.10] Younger than the mountains, growing like a breeze\n[00:59.76] Country Roads, take me home\n[01:04.86] To the place, I belong\n[01:10.18] West Virginia, Mountain mama\n[01:15.44] Take me home, Country Road\n[01:22.21] All my memories, gather 'round her\n[01:27.50] Miner's lady, strangers to blue water\n[01:34.09] Dark and dusty, painted on the sky\n[01:38.71] Misty taste of moonshine, tear drops in my eyes\n[01:43.33] Country Roads, take me home\n[01:48.45] To the place, I belong\n[01:53.77] West Virginia, Mountain mama\n[01:59.03] Take me home, Country Road\n[02:05.46] I hear her voice in the morning how she calls me,\n[02:10.42] The radio reminds me, of my home far away,\n[02:15.37] And driving down the road, I get 